    turnFlow: 'Partners play climbing combinations to empty hands, call Tichu bets, and use special cards such as Dragon, Phoenix, Dog, and Mah Jong. Points from captured cards and successful calls determine the score.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Big Two is a point-based shedding game played without a pre-hand monetary ante.',
      deal: 'The entire 52-card deck is distributed equally by the system dealer at the start of the round.',
      reveal_market: 'This is a closed-hand climbing game where all cards are held privately; no community market exists.',
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase or swap cards from any external area; they must succeed with their initial 13 cards.',
      buy_stock: 'The entire deck is distributed at once; no cards remain in stock to be purchased during play.',
      fold: 'Players must remain in the game until a winner has shed all cards to determine the penalty counts.',
      check: 'The game uses a climbing and passing structure rather than a vying structure with checks and bets.',
      call: 'There is no pot or bet to match in Big Two; competition is based on combination rankings.',
      bet: 'The game is scored via penalty points for cards remaining in hand rather than through wagering.',
      raise: 'There are no wagering rounds in this game, so the value of the deal cannot be increased via raises.',
      declare: 'Winning results are immediate upon playing the last card; no formal declaration phase is required.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands remain private until individual cards are played into climbing combos; no showdown occurs.',
      award_pot: 'Points are tallied on a scorecard after each hand; there is no physical pot of assets to award.',
      play_card: 'Must match the combination type and exceed the previous rank/suit.',
      draw: 'Each player receives thirteen cards at the start and no further drawing occurs during the play phase.',
      discard: 'Every card must be shed through valid climbing combinations; there is no separate discard or waste pile.',
      pass: 'Allowed at any time during the climbing phase.',
      bid: 'Big Two does not utilize a bidding system to determine the dealer, trump, or game objectives.',
      meld: 'This is a climbing game based on beating combinations rather than creating or laying down melds.',
      go_out: 'A player wins the round automatically upon playing their final combination from hand.',
